        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sarah Jacobson, Arthur Hiller\n- Places: Norwalk, Connecticut; New York City\n- Roles: independent filmmaker, television director, film director\n- Works: I Was a Teenage Serial Killer\n- Topics: underground film, no-budget film\n\nFacts:\n- Sarah Jacobson was born on August 25, 1971, in Norwalk, Connecticut.\n- Arthur Hiller was born on November 22, 1923.\n- Sarah Jacobson was an independent filmmaker who wrote, produced, and filmed her own movies.\n- Arthur Hiller was a Canadian-American television and film director who directed over 33 films during a 50-year career.\n- I Was a Teenage Serial Killer is an underground no-budget film written and directed by Sarah Jacobson, who was called \"The Queen of Underground Film.\"\n- Sarah Jacobson died on February 13, 2004, in New York City.\n- Arthur Hiller died on August 17, 2016.",
